data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":1430,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"input_transformations":[],"id":"resp_0b37d3f632b2946d016b048869471087d1ac52bbe204ff02fe","object":"response","created_at":1795459177,"completed_at":1795459214,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"Review the entire batch using only this experiment registry and applicant facts. Compare function, conditions, inputs and effects, not names. Search related capabilities before duplicate development when candidates are incomplete. Existing equivalent functions reuse their ID and learning duration; each applicant still studies individually. Reasonable missing mechanisms enter the existing current-conversation development handoff, not permanent rejection because no primitive currently exists. Propose the smallest executable version or feasible precursor, not an invented activity roadmap or fixed-era unlock.\nSpecify material/energy/time costs, prerequisites, dependencies, input/output conservation, exact references, work progress, interruption/resume/cancel/death/refund rules, ongoing processes, maintenance and real products/effects. No free stock, hidden-resource disclosure, consent or mastery. Actual participants must communicate and act independently. Code reuse must be recorded, not claimed as reinvention. Effects need observable events and reusable visual metadata; failed/incomplete actions cannot display success.\nEvaluate functional effects, experience and visuals separately. Short pleasure and slowly maintained satisfaction require real events, personal applicability, bounded amount/cap, decay/cooldown and functional deduplication. Verified information gain (including informative failure) may qualify; queries, requests, naming, registration and mastery never do. Familiar legitimate practice and social pa